   scrcpy-panel is a fork of ScrcpyRUST. The Rust client skeleton — the ADB
   layer, the scrcpy wire-protocol demuxer, the FFmpeg decoder wrapper, the
   control-message and input layers — originates from that project.

   Modifications made in scrcpy-panel (see git history for the full record):
     - Replaced the SDL2 window/renderer with a Slint user interface
     - Bumped the FFmpeg bindings from ffmpeg-next 8 to ffmpeg-next 9
     - Added the missing `libc` dependency required by the V4L2 sink
     - Removed development artifacts committed to the upstream repository
     - Added this NOTICE file and the Apache License 2.0 text, which the
       upstream repository declares in its README and Cargo.toml but does
       not ship as a file


2. scrcpy
   https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy
   Copyright (C) 2018 Genymobile
   Copyright (C) 2018-2026 Romain Vimont
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   scrcpy-panel speaks the scrcpy wire protocol and runs the unmodified
   scrcpy server (`scrcpy-server`) on the Android device. The client
   architecture — the module layout, the protocol framing, the control
   message format and the Android keycode mappings — derives from scrcpy.

   The scrcpy server binary is not redistributed as part of this repository;
   it is obtained from the upstream scrcpy release matching the protocol
   version this client implements.


